From f8b168ae3e65131e2d05c48b574ac04c19d57f0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: baverrr <342259467+baverrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:52:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Use the RavenOS glass theme for all alert and error dialogs

RavenOS is always dark, but apps on light themes still opened light
dialogs, such as Camera2's "critical permissions" error. Make every
framework dialog the dark glass dialog:

- Theme.Material.Light opens Theme.Material.Dialog(.Alert) as its
  dialogTheme and alertDialogTheme, and Theme.Material.Light.Dialog
  (with Light.Dialog.Alert, MinWidth, NoActionBar and FixedSize, which
  inherit from it by name) is based on Theme.Material.Dialog.
- Theme.DeviceDefault.Light.Dialog, .MinWidth, .NoActionBar,
  .NoActionBar.MinWidth, .FixedSize, .NoActionBar.FixedSize and
  .Light.Dialog.Alert are now the dark DeviceDefault dialog themes. That
  also covers the crash and "isn't responding" dialogs
  (Theme.DeviceDefault.Dialog.AppError) and SystemUI's dialogs.
- Dialogs use raven_card_radius corners in every DeviceDefault and
  Material theme, and dialog_background_material gets the thin
  raven_glass_stroke edge of the theme's cards.
- SystemUI's media output dialog uses the same corners and edge.

Colors come from the dark palette already pointed at raven_glass.xml:
raven_surface background, light text, raven_accent buttons. No public
resource changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
